{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED (Phase 1 / rebar-debug, analysis only — no code changed).\n\n## The mechanism\n\nThe only `cache_control` breakpoint rebar ever places is on the SYSTEM-prompt block (plus tool\ndefinitions). `capabilities.cache_settings_for` (src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py:333-355) sets\nexactly `anthropic_cache_instructions=True` + `anthropic_cache_tool_definitions=True` and its\ndocstring states outright that \"neither `*_cache_messages` nor `anthropic_cache` is touched\".\npydantic-ai honours that by putting `cache_control` on the last system-prompt block only\n(.venv/.../pydantic_ai/models/anthropic.py:1578-1616) and on the last tool (ibid. 1186-1194).\n\nFor BOTH failing call sites the marked system block is tiny and the real payload rides in the\nUSER message, after the breakpoint, where nothing is marked:\n\n* `coach_notes` — the `<!--volatile-->` marker sits at line 20 of the 22-line\n  src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_coach.md, so `prompts.resolve_prompt_cached`\n  (src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py:438-465) keeps only the 9-line stance prose as the stable\n  system prefix and routes `{{plan}}` into the user message.\n* the haiku sub-call is `enrich()` / ticket-digest (src/rebar/llm/enrich.py:82 binds\n  TRIVIAL_CLASS = claude-haiku-4-5; lines 94-98 render the prompt as `system_prompt` and pass the\n  whole ticket text as `instructions`).\n\nAnthropic SILENTLY declines to cache a breakpoint whose prefix is under the model minimum — no\nerror, `cache_creation=0`, `cache_read=0` — which is exactly the reported reading.\n\n## Experiment 1 — captured outbound request (one layer below the warning)\n\nHarness wrapped the httpx transport at the `_wrapped_transport` seam of\n`anthropic_model._build_retrying_anthropic_model` (src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py:95-161) and\ndumped the JSON body before it left the process. Real config, real runner, real prompts:\n\n```\nCOACH_NOTES  model=claude-opus-4-8 (config's default; the run used sonnet)\n  system block[0]  602 chars ~150 tokens   cache_control={'type':'ephemeral','ttl':'5m'}\n  tools: 0\n  user message   27712 chars ~6928 tokens  cache_control=None\n  markers present: [\"system[0]\"]\n\nENRICH/ticket-digest  model=claude-haiku-4-5\n  system block[0] 1909 chars ~477 tokens   cache_control={'type':'ephemeral','ttl':'5m'}\n  tools: 0\n  user message   25304 chars ~6326 tokens  cache_control=None\n  markers present: [\"system[0]\"]\n```\n\n## Experiment 2 — live A/B that discriminates size from the alternatives\n\nIdentical marker, identical large user message; only the marked prefix size varies\n(claude-haiku-4-5 and claude-sonnet-4-5, each called twice, `cache_creation`/`cache_read` read\noff `usage`):\n\n```\nhaiku-4-5   marked prefix  1193 tok -> write=0     read=0        NOT CACHED\nhaiku-4-5   marked prefix  2748 tok -> write=0     read=0        NOT CACHED\nhaiku-4-5   marked prefix  4749 tok -> write=4742  read=4742     CACHED\nhaiku-4-5   marked prefix  7182 tok -> cached\nsonnet-4-5  marked prefix   253 tok -> write=0     read=0        NOT CACHED\nsonnet-4-5  marked prefix  7930 tok -> write=7923                CACHED\n```\n\nThe empirical floor for both models sits between 2748 and 4749 tokens. rebar marks 150 and 477.\n\n## Hypotheses REJECTED\n\n* (a) \"these paths never place a cache_control breakpoint\" — REJECTED. The captured request shows\n  `cache_control` present on `system[0]` in both cases.\n* (b) \"the prefix is not stable between calls\" — REJECTED twice over. `cache_write=0` means no\n  write was ever attempted; an unstable-but-marked prefix would still write on every call. And the\n  marked block is byte-stable by construction: the coach's system prefix contains no per-run\n  variable (they all sit after `<!--volatile-->`), and enrich renders its prompt with `{}`.\n* \"caching is unavailable / provider-side\" — REJECTED: the same process cached fine for the\n  Pass-1 finders, which prepend `shared_plan_prefix(plan)` into the SYSTEM prompt\n  (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py:282,290), producing a multi-thousand-token marked prefix.\n  That is precisely the 5781-9385 cache_write rows in the report.\n\n## On CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS = 4096\n\nCausally involved, but not in the way the constant's docstring suggests, and it is not the cost\ndefect. Its VALUE is empirically about right for sonnet-4-5/haiku-4-5 (measured floor between\n2748 and 4749), so calling it \"the OPUS floor\" understates it. The real problem is the QUANTITY it\nis compared against: `warn_if_cache_ineffective` (src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:417-422) tests\n`usage[\"input_tokens\"]` — the TOTAL billed input — when the quantity that governs whether the\ncache engages is the size of the MARKED PREFIX. Both warnings are true positives, but only by\ncoincidence of the totals being above 4096; the same predicate applied to the marked prefix\n(150 / 477) would have named the cause directly.\n\n## Cost impact, and where a fix belongs (NOT implemented — 8415 owns llm/overlap, parity is owned\nelsewhere)\n\n* `coach_notes` is genuine, recoverable bleed: the plan is ALREADY in the Anthropic cache, written\n  by the Pass-1 finders that carry it in the system prefix. The coach re-sends the same plan in the\n  user message, a different slot, so it cannot hit that entry and re-pays full price every run.\n* `enrich`/ticket-digest is different in kind: its 6.3k user-message payload is one ticket's text,\n  unique per call, so even a message-level breakpoint would only ever WRITE, never READ. There is\n  no reusable prefix at that site at all.\n\nSo the fix belongs at the SHARED seam, not the call sites. `cache_settings_for`\n(capabilities.py:333-355) is the single place that decides breakpoint placement today and it\nexplicitly opts out of message-level caching; moving the payload back into the system prompt at\neach call site would be a direct reversal of story c6e5's stable-prefix split. Two shared-seam\noptions worth weighing: mark the last user content block (`anthropic_cache_messages`), or use\nAnthropic's automatic top-level `cache_control` (`anthropic_cache`, pydantic-ai\nanthropic.py:336-346), which places the breakpoint after the whole prompt. Either one needs a\nguard so a site like enrich, with no reusable prefix, does not pay write overhead for a read that\nnever comes."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785708399484831001,"uuid":"7aa7ee53-1df8-4fd8-8e05-34f6f52e6519"}